ct of the mandatory restart step.","evidence_ids":["cmd-00666fec348d4813","cmd-d838b133ae53426f","cmd-3e9c3c14e1d141ed","cmd-ee9103e7969b4197","cmd-53ca44961a9c4931","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task were directly demonstrated: a local-storage apk repository was built and served over HTTP via darkhttpd, the usual remote CDN was made unreachable via a hosts blackhole and confirmed unreachable at install time, mtr was successfully installed from the local repo under that condition, and normal configuration was restored afterward. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also fully satisfied with a coherent pre-restart baseline, reboot acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and post-restart recovery of the package, local repo data, and network config, cross-checked against the fixed global boot-identity snapshots. Hygiene is good but not perfect: a few bounded, failed busybox-httpd troubleshooting attempts and an unstopped darkhttpd daemon (cleared only incidentally by the reboot) and unconfirmed removal of .bak files are minor blemishes.","limitations":["No direct evidence that /etc/apk/repositories.bak and /etc/hosts.bak backup files were removed after use.","darkhttpd was not explicitly stopped during the restore step; its termination is inferred only from the absence of a port 8080 listener in the after_executor snapshot, not from a direct stop command.","prepare phase was disabled (alias of before_prepare), so preparation-specific comparison offers no additional signal beyond the before/after_executor comparison."]},"ttft_ms":28139,"type":"result","duration_ms":74513,"uuid":"72a64a65-faeb-4266-a9f1-d1d6184ad09b","ttft_stream_ms":2280,"time_to_request_ms":179,"first_content_frame_ms":2280,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
